From: Trijal Saha <97483939+Trijal08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] samsung-sit: take the carrier-config directory from udev only

The plugin compiled in /lib/firmware/google/s5400/carrierconfig as the
fallback for where it opens cfg.db. Where a device's vendor blobs land is a
packaging decision, not something a protocol plugin should know: the aport
that ships them is the one that knows where they went, and exynos-modem's
udev rule already sets ID_MM_SIT_CARRIER_CONFIG_DIRECTORY to exactly that
path. The compiled-in copy was a second, silently diverging source of truth.

So the property becomes the only source. With no property there is no
database path, which the modem already handles: carrier configuration
returns MM_CORE_ERROR_NOT_FOUND, "requires a database", and everything
else about the modem still comes up.

MM_SIT_ANNOUNCED_CARRIER_CONFIG_DIRECTORY stays. It is not a path anything
reads -- it is the value that goes on the wire in CARRIER_CONFIG_MANIFEST,
and the frame has to match the vendor RIL byte for byte. There is no
/vendor on this rootfs at all; exynos-modem's RFS server re-roots whatever
the CP opens under it onto the real files.

After this the plugin holds no device-specific path: a grep for quoted
absolute paths finds only that wire constant and /etc/os-release, and
"komodo" survives only in comments recording where a capture came from.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XzdpD3EoDuxNrEps73GD56
diff -ruN a/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-broadband-modem-samsung-sit.h b/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-broadband-modem-samsung-sit.h
--- a/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-broadband-modem-samsung-sit.h	2026-11-08 09:02:12.627942591 -0500
+++ b/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-broadband-modem-samsung-sit.h	2026-11-08 10:52:12.318930475 -0500
@@ -17,11 +17,14 @@
  * exynos-modem's RFS server re-roots whatever the CP opens onto the real
  * files, so nothing has to exist at this path.
  *
- * LOCAL is where the plugin itself opens cfg.db, which it has to be able to
- * read directly. A udev rule may override it for a different layout.
+ * Where the plugin opens cfg.db is deliberately not here. That is a property
+ * of how a particular device packages its vendor blobs, so it comes from the
+ * port's ID_MM_SIT_CARRIER_CONFIG_DIRECTORY and nowhere else; the aport that
+ * ships the blobs is the one that knows where they landed. Without it the
+ * modem still comes up, and the carrier configuration reports that it needs a
+ * database.
  */
 #define MM_SIT_ANNOUNCED_CARRIER_CONFIG_DIRECTORY "/vendor/firmware/carrierconfig"
-#define MM_SIT_DEFAULT_CARRIER_CONFIG_DIRECTORY   "/lib/firmware/google/s5400/carrierconfig"
 
 #define MM_TYPE_BROADBAND_MODEM_SAMSUNG_SIT            (mm_broadband_modem_samsung_sit_get_type ())
 #define MM_BROADBAND_MODEM_SAMSUNG_SIT(obj)            (G_TYPE_CHECK_INSTANCE_CAST ((obj), MM_TYPE_BROADBAND_MODEM_SAMSUNG_SIT, MMBroadbandModemSamsungSit))
diff -ruN a/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-plugin-samsung-sit.c b/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-plugin-samsung-sit.c
--- a/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-plugin-samsung-sit.c	2026-11-08 09:02:12.614621885 -0500
+++ b/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-plugin-samsung-sit.c	2026-11-08 10:52:12.318957495 -0500
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
               GError       **error)
 {
     g_autofree gchar *database = NULL;
-    const gchar      *directory = MM_SIT_DEFAULT_CARRIER_CONFIG_DIRECTORY;
+    const gchar      *directory = NULL;
     gboolean          use_proxy = FALSE;
     gint              logical_stack = -1;
     GList            *l;
@@ -44,6 +44,8 @@
         if (!mm_port_probe_is_sit (probe))
             continue;
         port = mm_port_probe_peek_port (probe);
+        /* The only source for this: no path to a device's vendor blobs is
+         * compiled in. */
         configured_directory = mm_kernel_device_get_property (
             port, "ID_MM_SIT_CARRIER_CONFIG_DIRECTORY");
         if (configured_directory && configured_directory[0])
@@ -67,7 +69,8 @@
         break;
     }
 
-    database = g_build_filename (directory, "cfg.db", NULL);
+    if (directory)
+        database = g_build_filename (directory, "cfg.db", NULL);
     return MM_BASE_MODEM (mm_broadband_modem_samsung_sit_new (
         uid, physdev, drivers, mm_plugin_get_name (self), vendor, product, database,
         use_proxy, logical_stack));
